### **Identified Risks for Each Risk Class**

#### **Risk 1:**
**Description:**
The **rolling cylindrical object** may **enter the road**, posing a collision risk to the **following vehicle** (or any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction). The **fog** further reduces reaction time.

**Severity Score:** **0.85** (High risk due to visibility and object motion)

#### **Risk 2:**
**Description:**
The **pedestrian** standing near the **truck’s rear** could be **unaware of the rolling objects** and may **step into the road**, leading to a collision with the **truck or following vehicle**.

**Severity Score:** **0.75** (Moderate-high risk due to pedestrian proximity and object motion)

#### **Risk 3:**
**Description:**
The **rectangular object (biohazard crate)** rolling onto the road could **damage infrastructure** (e.g., road signs, traffic lights) or **injure pedestrians** if it hits them.

**Severity Score:** **0.65** (Moderate risk due to potential secondary hazards)

#### **Risk 4:**
**Description:**
The **following vehicle** may **not detect the truck or obstacles** due to **fog**, leading to a **rear-end collision** or **failure to yield**.

**Severity Score:** **0.80** (High risk due to visibility impairment)

#### **Risk 5:**
**Description:**
The **truck’s blind spot** (due to its size and the pedestrian’s position) increases the risk of **pedestrian-vehicle collision** if the pedestrian moves unexpectedly.

**Severity Score:** **0.70** (Moderate-high risk due to blind spot and pedestrian movement)

---
### **Summary of Key Risks**
| **Risk** | **Severity (0-1)** | **Primary Concern** |
|----------|-------------------|---------------------|
| Rolling cylindrical object on road | 0.85 | Collision with following vehicles |
| Pedestrian near truck rear | 0.75 | Pedestrian-vehicle collision |
| Following vehicle in fog | 0.80 | Rear-end collision |
| Biohazard crate on road | 0.65 | Infrastructure damage |
| Truck blind spot risk | 0.70 | Pedestrian collision |

This scene presents **multiple high-severity risks** due to **reduced visibility, rolling obstacles, and pedestrian proximity**. An autonomous vehicle must **prioritize obstacle detection, pedestrian tracking, and adaptive speed control** to mitigate these hazards.